# --- Database ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development: SQLite file (file path relative to prisma/). DEV ONLY.
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"

# PRODUCTION: set Turso (libSQL) — a managed, server-based, scalable
# SQLite-compatible DB. Without these the app REFUSES to start in production
# (NODE_ENV=production), so you don't accidentally send real customers onto an
# ephemeral file DB that loses data on every deploy. Create with:
#   turso db create <your-shop>-db && turso db tokens create <your-shop>-db
# See DEPLOY.md §2. (Deliberate self-host on a persistent volume: ALLOW_SQLITE_IN_PRODUCTION=1)
# TURSO_DATABASE_URL="libsql://<your-shop>-db.turso.io"
# TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=""

# Auth.js — generate a secret with: npx auth secret
AUTH_SECRET="replace-me-with-a-random-string"

# Canonical site URL for Auth.js callback/redirect URLs. The engine sets
# trustHost:true so self-hosted prod (next start / Docker / non-Vercel) works
# out of the box — but in production you should ALSO pin AUTH_URL to your real
# origin so a spoofed Host header can't redirect auth flows. On Vercel this is
# auto-detected and can be left unset. Example: https://shop.example.com
# AUTH_URL="https://your-domain.com"

# Admin start-password (seed). If set, `prisma db seed` creates the admin with
# THIS password. If UNSET, the seed generates a strong random password, prints it
# ONCE in the seed output, and forces a change on first admin login (/admin/konto).
# There is never a hardcoded default. Set this to pick your own, or leave it unset.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD="choose-a-strong-admin-password"

# Demo-only: admin password used by the /api/admin/reset-demo-data endpoint on the
# demo canaries. Set per demo deploy for a known demo login; unset = a random one
# is generated (password-login then needs this env, or use magic-link).
# DEMO_ADMIN_PASSWORD=""

# Anthropic API key for the storefront AI assistant (/api/assistant/chat).
# Without this, the endpoint returns 503 and the chat window shows a friendly error.
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com/
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""

# Unsplash API key for image search from admin chat (images.search_unsplash).
# Without this, the AI cannot suggest images for new products.
# Get a free dev key at https://unsplash.com/oauth/applications (50 req/hour)
UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY=""

# Phase 4: Stripe (real payment via webhook). Set via /admin/integrations
# instead of env if you prefer database-backed config.
# Without keys = mock checkout (no real money). Test keys (sk_test_…) =
# Stripe test mode. Before you accept REAL payments you must use
# LIVE keys (sk_live_…) from an activated Stripe account. See DEPLOY.md §5.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=""
# STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=""
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
# Optional Track T7 recurring billing price. Must be a Stripe Price ID
# (price_...) for a recurring Price/Product in Stripe Billing.
# STRIPE_SUBSCRIPTION_PRICE_ID=""

# Phone.inc webhook shared secret (plugin: phone-widget, features.phoneWidget).
# Optional. Unset = the /api/phone/webhook endpoint accepts any caller (its
# handlers are no-ops today). Set it to require authentication: callers must
# then present the value as header `x-phone-inc-signature: <secret>` OR as the
# `?token=<secret>` query param on the webhook URL, else they get 401.
# PHONE_INC_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

# Phase 4: Resend email service (replaces PreviewMailer in production).
# RESEND_API_KEY=""

# Phase 4: Sentry error tracking (critical for production). No-op without DSN.
# Server-side DSN (private):
# SENTRY_DSN=""
# Client-side DSN (public, bundled in JS):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=""
# Build-time source map upload (set in Vercel project env, not locally).
# Generate token at https://sentry.io/settings/auth-tokens/ with scopes
# project:releases + org:read.
# SENTRY_ORG=""
# SENTRY_PROJECT=""
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=""

# Phase 4: Vercel Cron auth-secret for /api/cron/reconcile-stripe.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# CRON_SECRET=""

# Phase 11: Upstash Redis Rate Limiting. Required to rate-limit /api endpoints.
# Create a free Redis database at https://console.upstash.com/
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=""
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=""

# Phase 10: Google Search Console verification meta-tag content value.
# The value from <meta name="google-site-verification" content="...">. Set it
# in Search Console under "URL prefix property → HTML tag verification method".
# GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=""

# Phase 10: Google Analytics 4 measurement ID. Format G-XXXXXXXXXX.
# The script loads ONLY after the customer has accepted analytics cookies via
# the consent banner (Google Consent Mode v2 — anonymous pings until consent).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID=""

# Phase 10: Gemini API key for auto-generated alt text/SEO/GEO metadata on
# uploads. The /api/cron/media-ai cron uses the same key as the /admin/integrations
# admin DB value — env fallback when the DB key is not set.
# GOOGLE_GEMINI_API_KEY=""

# Phase 10 Slice 7c: date (ISO) from which post-purchase review prompts are sent.
# Protects history from getting "thanks for your purchase" emails on old orders on
# first activation. Set it to the deploy time when the reviews flag is flipped to true.
# Format: "2026-05-25T00:00:00Z". Unset = the cron no-ops (safe default).
# REVIEW_PROMPTS_FROM=""

# ── v0.10.0 -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Firecrawl: web-scraping API. Powers the product scraper (/admin/produkter/scrape,
# Track F), the design importer (/admin/design-import, Track I) AND Hoptify's real
# "import from Shopify" (/admin/hoptify). Without a key all three fall back to
# manual/demo mode. Get a key at https://www.firecrawl.dev/
# FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=""

# Vercel Blob read/write token. Used by the Hoptify logo generator
# (/admin/indstillinger → "Generate with Gemini") to upload the generated
# raster logo. Generated in the Vercel dashboard → Storage → Blob → Tokens.
# (On Vercel it is typically set automatically when a Blob store is linked.)
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=""

# "Sign in with GitHub" (features.githubAuth). Optional OAuth login alongside
# magic-link. Create an OAuth App at https://github.com/settings/developers with
# callback https://<your-domain>/api/auth/callback/github, and set the flag true in
# brand.config.ts. The button only shows when BOTH the flag AND both keys are set.
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=""
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# "Continue with Google" (features.googleAuth). Customer OAuth login alongside
# magic-link. Callback: https://<your-domain>/api/auth/callback/google
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# Note on reused keys in v0.10.0:
# - GOOGLE_GEMINI_API_KEY (above): now ALSO powers the Hoptify logo generator
#   (gemini-2.5-flash-image), in addition to media-AI + voice.
# - CRON_SECRET (above): now ALSO gates /api/cron/{backup,abandoned-cart,
#   cleanup-expired-tokens,audit-retention,seo-snapshot} — not just stripe-reconcile.
# - UPSTASH_REDIS_* (above): now ALSO used by Track H admin redirects (proxy cache).
# - Stripe Tax (features.stripeTax) + Google Search Console OAuth (SEO Autopilot)
#   are configured via /admin/integrations (DB), not via env.

# ── Cartwright Plus (membership) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Plus access key from cartwright.app/pricing (cw_plus_v1.…). Env-only in v1;
# status + activation live in /admin/plus. A missing/canceled key never
# disables the site — see docs/plus.md.
# CARTWRIGHT_PLUS_KEY=""

# Optional override of the built-in Plus verification public key (base64 SPKI
# DER or PEM). Only for testing/key rotation — normally ships in the engine.
# CARTWRIGHT_PLUS_PUBLIC_KEY=""

# Optional Stripe customer-portal link shown on /admin/plus ("Billing").
# Without it the page points members to the portal link in their purchase email.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PORTAL_URL=""
